# DTF tier manifest: verify-skip-client-verified-oci  (artifact-keeper#6468)
#
# THE CHANGE (#6468)
#   Serve-time SHA-256 verification costs about 7 CPU-seconds per GiB on a
#   core without SHA extensions and caps one verified stream near 140 MB/s.
#   DOWNLOAD_VERIFY_SKIP_CLIENT_VERIFIED=oci (opt-in; default unset) turns it
#   off on OCI blob GETs only, where every client checks the digest it pulled.
#
# THE ORACLE (oracle.sh), with the knob set (profile
# verify.skip-client-verified-oci):
#   FIX:     a corrupted OCI blob (one byte flipped on disk) is served 200 in
#            full, unverified, so its body does not hash to the digest the
#            client asked for (the client is the check). Main ignores the knob
#            and answers 502 STORED_OBJECT_INTEGRITY.
#   CONTROL: a corrupted generic artifact on the same backend is still
#            refused (502), so the knob reaches no other route; an intact blob
#            is served whole on both images.
# The default (knob unset): verify-skip-client-verified-oci-default runs this
# oracle without the option, where a corrupted blob is still 502; and
# storage-integrity and oci-manifest-scrub still verify OCI blobs.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem verify.skip-client-verified-oci"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
